<title>GERMANY: EMI council meeting started, no comment on agenda.</title>
<headline>EMI council meeting started, no comment on agenda.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The regular meeting of the European Monetary Institute (EMI) council began on Tuesday at around 0800 GMT, the EMI said.</p>
<p>As usual, the EMI made no comment on the agenda for the meeting.</p>
<p>The council comprises 15 EU central bank governors and the EMI president Alexandre Lamfalussy. All EU states were represented at the meeting, the EMI said.</p>
<p>The meeting generally runs through around 1400 GMT.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy is scheduled to hold a news conference at 1500 GMT to mark the release of the EMI's third annual report.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
